  "overview_markdown": "GoClaw is a ground-up Go reimplementation of OpenClaw, repositioned as a multi-tenant AI agent gateway rather than a personal assistant. It ships as a single binary backed by PostgreSQL 18, supports 20+ LLM providers and 7 messaging channels, and exposes WebSocket APIs with OpenTelemetry tracing built in. The core pitch is deploying teams of agents at scale with tenant isolation and a 5-layer security model.\n\nThe recent commit history shows serious security and reliability engineering: subagent tool policies now inherit the parent's exec/read/write deny rules (closing a sandbox-escape path), skill slash commands are filtered by per-agent grants, skill archive imports sanitize paths against traversal, and team task dispatch deadlocks were fixed. This suggests an actively hardened codebase with real production usage.\n\nCompared to OpenClaw, GoClaw trades the massive skill ecosystem and permissive licensing for stronger multi-tenancy, native concurrency, and lower resource usage. Its CC BY-NC 4.0 license is the biggest caveat — commercial deployments require caution. It fits operators building internal agent platforms more than hobbyists wanting a personal lobster assistant.",
